 8. As HunchLab does, which has been deployed in several US states.
 9. Note also that it is possible to combine the pro tanto and prima facie accounts of the value 
of the window of moral opportunity by holding that the window is not always valuable, 
and when it is, its value may be outweighed by others. See Noggle (2018) for a recent appli-
cation of this distinction.
 10. Of course, preparatory offences are offences. Arrests of those preparing to commit 
terrorist acts are, in that sense, not pre- emptive. A cleaner example will involve a case in 
which a person has not committed an act that is justifiably criminalized. See below for fur-
ther discussion.
